00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.700
- Hey guys, today we're gonna
talk about a very fascinating

00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:04.723
interesting topic, zinc.

00:00:05.630 --> 00:00:09.150
Now because zinc is so vital for your body

00:00:09.150 --> 00:00:11.900
and it's just a fascinating
mineral, I created three parts.

00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:14.950
First thing you need to
know is two billion people

00:00:14.950 --> 00:00:17.370
on this planet are deficient in zinc.

00:00:17.370 --> 00:00:20.533
That's crazy. That's a lot
of people that are deficient.

00:00:21.410 --> 00:00:23.010
I would imagine it's even more than that

00:00:23.010 --> 00:00:26.490
as far as having a subclinical deficiency

00:00:26.490 --> 00:00:29.490
and as we go through this you'll
see what I'm talking about.

00:00:29.490 --> 00:00:32.030
One thing about zinc is
the body does not store it

00:00:32.030 --> 00:00:34.080
so you have to constantly
actually take it in.

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:35.050
and it's a trace mineral

00:00:35.050 --> 00:00:38.530
which means that we need
it in smaller amounts

00:00:38.530 --> 00:00:41.540
compared to things like
potassium and it's essential.

00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:43.320
So what does it mainly do?

00:00:43.320 --> 00:00:48.320
It acts as a cofactor
for over 1000 enzymes.

00:00:49.220 --> 00:00:51.460
So you have all these
chemical reactions going on

00:00:51.460 --> 00:00:55.610
at the cellular level
with DNA turning into RNA

00:00:55.610 --> 00:00:57.780
which is the kind of the blueprints

00:00:57.780 --> 00:01:00.710
turning into the copy of those blueprints

00:01:00.710 --> 00:01:04.960
and the transcription and the
interpretation and all that

00:01:04.960 --> 00:01:08.160
and the building of
proteins all needs zinc.

00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:10.910
So the enzymes are
those things in the body

00:01:10.910 --> 00:01:14.640
that do all the work and
they need certain minerals

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:16.820
to accomplish their job.

00:01:16.820 --> 00:01:20.890
10% of all human protein is bound to zinc.

00:01:20.890 --> 00:01:23.810
It's a vital, vital nutrient.

00:01:23.810 --> 00:01:26.950
It's the most common deficiency in crops

00:01:26.950 --> 00:01:28.500
so I wanna read something here.

00:01:30.160 --> 00:01:32.968
Scarcity in the soil,
deficiency of micronutrients

00:01:32.968 --> 00:01:35.380
that are essential for plant growth,

00:01:35.380 --> 00:01:38.010
can lead to a lower crop yield.

00:01:38.010 --> 00:01:41.900
During the past decade soil
micronutrient deficiencies

00:01:41.900 --> 00:01:45.240
have been ascertained primarily for zinc.

00:01:45.240 --> 00:01:48.810
To a lesser extent, boron and molybdenum.

00:01:48.810 --> 00:01:53.810
Soil deficiencies of zinc
are widespread in Asia.

00:01:54.010 --> 00:01:56.470
Scarcity in feed and
food and human nutrition,

00:01:56.470 --> 00:01:59.350
zinc deficiency is the most well known

00:01:59.350 --> 00:02:02.020
micronutrient deficiency.

00:02:02.020 --> 00:02:04.260
Zinc deficiency can
cause disorders in humans

00:02:04.260 --> 00:02:06.663
such as retarded growth in children.

00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:11.120
We talked about it estimated
of 1/3 of the population

00:02:11.120 --> 00:02:13.190
is at risk for zinc deficiency.

00:02:13.190 --> 00:02:15.520
It is the fifth most important risk factor

00:02:15.520 --> 00:02:17.800
for disease in developing countries.

00:02:17.800 --> 00:02:20.520
Scarcity of mineral
deficiencies of micronutrients

00:02:20.520 --> 00:02:23.040
in agricultural soils can be replenished

00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:24.690
with mined minerals.

00:02:24.690 --> 00:02:27.270
And then they talk about
a lot of these minerals

00:02:27.270 --> 00:02:30.930
are used exclusively for
industrial applications,

00:02:30.930 --> 00:02:33.970
not crops, livestock or for humans.

00:02:33.970 --> 00:02:36.620
The mineral reserves
in relation to the use

00:02:36.620 --> 00:02:39.490
seem to be most restricted for zinc.

00:02:39.490 --> 00:02:41.850
At the current level of
production of mining,

00:02:41.850 --> 00:02:46.030
we have a reserve for
approximately another 21 years.

00:02:46.030 --> 00:02:48.290
So at that point I don't
know what's gonna happen.

00:02:48.290 --> 00:02:50.140
Priorities should be given to zinc

00:02:50.140 --> 00:02:52.970
because zinc deficiencies
are already occurring

00:02:52.970 --> 00:02:56.360
in food chains in a
large part of the world.

00:02:56.360 --> 00:02:57.453
Now on top of that,

00:02:58.710 --> 00:03:03.340
glyphosate as in GMO foods, Roundup Ready,

00:03:03.340 --> 00:03:05.430
acts as a major chelator

00:03:05.430 --> 00:03:09.150
to bind and block zinc and other minerals.

00:03:09.150 --> 00:03:10.840
Now I couldn't find the data currently,

00:03:10.840 --> 00:03:15.840
but in 2007 they were
putting 80,000 metric tons

00:03:16.940 --> 00:03:19.650
of glyphosate into the environment.

00:03:19.650 --> 00:03:21.100
Don't worry, it gets worse.

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:22.910
Alright so now let's get into the symptoms

00:03:22.910 --> 00:03:25.180
of what happens when
you're zinc deficient.

00:03:25.180 --> 00:03:27.120
Growth retardation.

00:03:27.120 --> 00:03:31.880
So if you're pregnant,
if you're breastfeeding,

00:03:31.880 --> 00:03:33.360
make sure that you're taking

00:03:33.360 --> 00:03:35.270
the trace minerals including zinc

00:03:35.270 --> 00:03:38.280
to maximize growth of that child.

00:03:38.280 --> 00:03:40.920
Loss of taste and/or smell.

00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:43.740
A lowered immune system

00:03:43.740 --> 00:03:46.790
which we'll get into in the next video.

00:03:46.790 --> 00:03:50.180
Prostate/testosterone issues.

00:03:50.180 --> 00:03:53.790
Skin problems, major depression.

00:03:53.790 --> 00:03:57.610
Zinc is intimately involved
in insulin production.

00:03:57.610 --> 00:04:00.393
Another side effect of zinc
deficiency is diarrhea.

00:04:01.730 --> 00:04:04.300
Eye problems, delayed healing,

00:04:04.300 --> 00:04:07.700
ulcers of the mouth, of
the digestive system.

00:04:07.700 --> 00:04:09.210
Zinc is a really good remedy

00:04:09.210 --> 00:04:11.440
for ulcers of the stomach as well.

00:04:11.440 --> 00:04:14.163
Macular degeneration related to age,

00:04:15.280 --> 00:04:16.960
inflammation in general.

00:04:16.960 --> 00:04:19.610
Zinc is a natural anti-inflammatory

00:04:19.610 --> 00:04:22.420
and it's a very powerful
antioxidant as well

00:04:22.420 --> 00:04:24.050
and I'm going to talk about
some of these other things

00:04:24.050 --> 00:04:26.250
in more detail in the
next couple of videos.

00:04:26.250 --> 00:04:27.780
The foods that are highest in zinc

00:04:27.780 --> 00:04:31.430
are oysters, beef, crab and
pumpkin seeds by the way.

00:04:31.430 --> 00:04:32.800
Now there's other things
that will decrease

00:04:32.800 --> 00:04:34.090
your absorption of zinc.

00:04:34.090 --> 00:04:35.970
If you had a gastric bypass surgery,

00:04:35.970 --> 00:04:39.330
if you had any type of digestive damage

00:04:39.330 --> 00:04:43.163
like IBS, Crohn's, diverticulitis,

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:46.840
you've had a lot of antibiotics.
That can create a problem.

00:04:46.840 --> 00:04:50.420
Liver disease, cirrhosis,
things like that.

00:04:50.420 --> 00:04:52.370
And also if you have lower stomach acid.

00:04:52.370 --> 00:04:54.620
So many people don't
have enough stomach acid

00:04:54.620 --> 00:04:58.103
because you need this acid
to absorb these minerals.

00:04:58.940 --> 00:05:00.340
How do you know if you're deficient?

00:05:00.340 --> 00:05:02.170
Well if you have heartburn,

00:05:02.170 --> 00:05:04.120
chances are you're deficient
in the acid that you need

00:05:04.120 --> 00:05:05.060
to absorb the minerals

00:05:05.060 --> 00:05:07.990
and especially if you're
taking an antiacid.

00:05:07.990 --> 00:05:10.180
Phytates or phytic acid,

00:05:10.180 --> 00:05:12.670
that would be in grains, whole grains.

00:05:12.670 --> 00:05:15.653
It's in the bran or the fiber
of whole grains and legumes.

00:05:16.790 --> 00:05:21.780
And this compound actually
blocks the absorption of zinc.

00:05:21.780 --> 00:05:23.710
So it's actually kinda like a chelator.

00:05:23.710 --> 00:05:26.033
It binds it very similar to glyphosate.

00:05:27.290 --> 00:05:29.870
Diabetes. Having high blood sugar

00:05:29.870 --> 00:05:33.430
because a high carb diet
will deplete zinc as well.

00:05:33.430 --> 00:05:34.670
So we're living in this environment

00:05:34.670 --> 00:05:37.870
that it's making it very hard to get zinc

00:05:37.870 --> 00:05:40.850
with the GMO foods, the high carb diets,

00:05:40.850 --> 00:05:43.360
with the soil becoming depleted

00:05:43.360 --> 00:05:45.470
and with all the pre-existing
digestive problems

00:05:45.470 --> 00:05:48.560
that we normally have, not
to mention low stomach acids

00:05:48.560 --> 00:05:50.360
because I really wanted
to bring up your awareness

00:05:50.360 --> 00:05:53.750
of these connections
between these problems

00:05:53.750 --> 00:05:55.680
and a simple trace mineral.

00:05:55.680 --> 00:05:57.130
Alright let's go to part two.

00:05:58.400 --> 00:06:00.290
So if you're enjoying this content,

00:06:00.290 --> 00:06:01.760
go ahead and share it with someone

